NOTICE

This work derives from the "speedtest" package for pfSense software by Marcello
Coutinho, distributed as part of Unofficial-pfSense-packages:

    https://github.com/marcelloc/Unofficial-pfSense-packages

As required by Section 4(b) of the Apache License, the following changes were
made to the Apache-licensed files:

  * diag_speedtest.php: the measurement is now displayed locally. The original
    passed --share unconditionally and rendered the result as nothing but the
    image Ookla returns, so a speed test could not be run without publishing
    it. Sharing is now a checkbox that defaults to off, the download, upload,
    latency, server and ISP are read out of the JSON and shown in a table, and
    the shared URL -- when there is one -- is validated and escaped rather than
    interpolated straight into an <img src>.

  * diag_speedtest.php: the variables backing the form are initialised, which
    silences a set of undefined-variable warnings on every page load under
    PHP 8.

  * Packaging: the package is built and installed as a real
    pfSense-pkg-SpeedTest rather than by copying files into place, so that it
    appears in and can be removed from System > Package Manager. See
    docs/PACKAGING.md.
